    question: "What is a Zettelkasten and do I need it?",
    answer:
      "<strong>Zettelkasten</strong> is a note-taking method focusing on atomic notes (one idea per note) connected via links to build a \"second brain.\" Apps like <strong>Obsidian</strong>, <strong>Roam Research</strong>, and <strong>Logseq</strong> are designed for this approach. You don't need it - simple folders and search work fine for most people. But if you're a researcher, writer, or knowledge worker building complex ideas, Zettelkasten is powerful.",
